WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:04.790
The Halloween franchise has had so many twists
and turns that trying to sort out the story

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:06.220
can be a little confusing.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:07.120
No worries, though.

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.460
We've laid out the whole timeline in detail.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:13.580
From that first night of terror to Michael's
bloody return, here's the entire Halloween

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.520
story finally explained.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.280
Halloween opens on Halloween night in 1963.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:23.380
Judith Myers should be babysitting her six-year-old
brother, Michael, but what she's actually

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:25.080
doing is making out with her boyfriend.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.680
So Michael decides he's going to spend his
evening doing some killing.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.160
After slaughtering his sister, he's institutionalized,
and his psychiatrist, Dr. Sam Loomis, becomes

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:38.200
convinced that Michael is pure evil and should
never be allowed back into the world.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.860
"I told everybody!

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:40.740
Nobody listened!"

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:45.880
But, in 1978, Michael escapes and heads back
to his hometown, looking to pick up right

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:46.800
where he left off.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:50.900
When he gets home, he finds high schooler
Laurie Strode hanging around, so of course

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.480
he decides to make her and her friends his
next targets.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:57.320
For the rest of the night, Michael stalks
and kills Laurie's friends, one by one.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:01.320
But Laurie is stronger than he gives her credit
for, and she manages to fend him off long

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:05.610
enough to allow Loomis to arrive on the scene
and shoot him six times, knocking him off

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:07.500
a balcony and onto the ground below.

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:11.720
That same night, Laurie is taken to Haddonfield
Memorial Hospital.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.660
Michael survives his fall from the balcony,
and follows Laurie because he's not one to

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.000
let his victims get away.

00:01:17.149 --> 00:01:19.700
It's also discovered that Laurie is, surprise!

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:20.719
Michael's younger sister.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.980
"That girl, that Strode girl.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:25.040
That's Michael Myers' sister."

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:30.100
And Michael is, even bigger surprise! possibly
being kept alive because of a Samhain curse.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:35.000
Michael wanders through the hospital in search
of Laurie, killing anyone and everyone that

00:01:35.009 --> 00:01:40.130
gets in his way, while Loomis starts his inevitable
descent into madness, trying to convince anyone

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:43.160
within earshot of Michael's evil immortality.

00:01:43.389 --> 00:01:48.680
In a final confrontation, Michael stabs Loomis
in the stomach, but not before Loomis sets

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:50.300
the hospital up to explode.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:54.220
Laurie gets out in time, but Michael and Loomis
are trapped inside when the building goes

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:54.960
up in flames.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:59.320
Michael Myers takes a backseat in Halloween
3, which takes place a few days prior to the

00:01:59.320 --> 00:01:59.820
holiday.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.020
When a man is killed in a northern California
hospital by a group of mysterious, well-dressed

00:02:04.039 --> 00:02:08.340
men, Dan Challis,the doctor in charge of his
care, takes it upon himself to try and solve

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:08.940
the case.

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:14.040
He traces the crime all the way back to Silver
Shamrock Novelties and a man named Conal Cochran,

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.220
who's somehow managed to steal a piece of
Stonehenge.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:21.360
He plans to use it as part of a sacrifice
involving children and a trio of Halloween

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:25.100
masks, with the goal of reclaiming the Samhain
holiday for witches.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:27.620
But Dan thwarts Cochran's plan, for the most
part.

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:32.580
There are robots, killer bugs, and the possibility
of a whole lot of child death, but no Michael

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:33.080
Myers.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:38.560
A decade after the hospital explosion, Michael
awakens from a coma, just in time to hunt

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:40.040
his niece, Jamie, on Halloween.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:44.460
Jamie, as it happens, is the seven-year-old
daughter of Laurie, who died in a car accident.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:48.880
Jamie's currently living with another family,
but her true lineage isn't a secret, so she's

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:50.160
bullied pretty heavily.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.620
"I don't need to wear a stupid costume."

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:54.980
"That's because everyday is Halloween in Jamie's
house.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.040
Right, Jamie?

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:57.240
'Cause your uncle is the Boogeyman."

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:02.120
Halloween 4 is a pretty straightforward slasher
flick, in that the bulk of it consists of

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:06.780
Michael Myers killing a bunch of poorly developed
characters in the most ridiculous ways imaginable.

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:11.620
But eventually, Loomis returns, because he's
somehow also managed to survive that hospital

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:16.290
explosion, and he helps Jamie defeat her uncle
with the help of a town lynch mob.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:20.380
Sadly, it seems as though psychopathy runs
in the family, because after Michael falls

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:24.040
through a mine shaft, Jamie tries to kill
her foster mother with a pair of scissors.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:29.220
Michael, wounded from the attempt on his life
in Halloween 4, crawls into a cave and immediately

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:30.100
passes out.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:33.900
He wakes up on Halloween Eve a year later,
in the care of another cave dweller.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:37.520
Michael kills him and sets course for his
niece, who's been living as a mute at the

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:39.760
Haddonfield Children's Clinic for the last
year.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:43.600
It's clear Jamie and Michael are connected
on a deeper level than just blood.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:48.580
The two are psychically paired, so everything
Michael does from here on out, Jamie sees.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:52.870
After his killing spree, Jamie tries to appeal
to his emotions, but Michael isn't interested

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:54.380
in anything other than killing.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:59.620
"In my heart, I knew that Hell would not have
him."

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:02.120
Loomis swoops in, but winds up suffering a
stroke.

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:06.700
There's no hero here, just a random set of
circumstances that leads to Michael's arrest.

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:10.681
In the end, a strange Man in Black who's been
following Michael this entire time comes to

00:04:10.681 --> 00:04:12.240
the police station to retrieve him.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:16.940
Six years later, we learn that the Man in
Black is the leader of a Druid cult that's

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:20.380
connected to Michael on account of a mark
he has on the inside of his wrist.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:24.580
Turns out, it's related to the so-called "curse
of Thorn," the thing responsible for both

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:28.639
Michael's immortality and his insatiable desire
to kill his family.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:31.220
"Michael's work isn't done in Haddonfield.

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:35.920
And soon, very soon, he'll come home."

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:40.200
Jamie, now 14, has delivered a baby in the
captivity of the cult.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:43.969
Immediately after giving birth, she tries
to escape the cult's clutches and outrun her

00:04:43.969 --> 00:04:44.600
uncle.

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:46.780
She fails, and Michael kills her in a barn.

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:51.000
The rest of the film shifts focus to Tommy
Doyle, the now adult boy that Laurie Strode

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:51.960
used to babysit.

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:55.380
He's obsessed with the curse of Thorn, and
with the old Myers home in general.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:58.910
Eventually, thanks to his help, Loomis is
able to take Michael down.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:04:59.720
Or is he?

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:05.260
Laurie Strode makes her return to the franchise
with Halloween H20: 20 Years Later, a film

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:09.200
that gets back to basics, effectively wiping
out everything that's happened after Halloween

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:09.700
II.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:13.879
Michael Myers is still family, but Laurie
is alive, having faked her death, and she's

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:17.700
working as the headmistress of her son John's
private boarding school in California.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:22.460
Michael reappears 20 years after that hospital
explosion and manages to track Laurie down

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:25.400
by way of an old file one of Loomis' colleagues
had on hand.

00:05:25.629 --> 00:05:30.000
In spite of her overprotective nature, Laurie
can't protect John and his friends from Michael's

00:05:30.009 --> 00:05:34.069
wrath, and on Halloween night, the masked
killer stalks and kills pretty much everyone

00:05:34.069 --> 00:05:36.280
at the school before Laurie can subdue him.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:38.560
"He's dead.

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:39.940
He's dead."

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:43.600
Laurie doesn't stop there, though.

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:47.810
She hijacks the coroner's van with Michael's
body, sends the slasher through the windshield,

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:50.420
pins him to a fence, and then takes an ax
to his head.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:55.380
All these years later, Laurie has finally
gotten her revenge, except for one tiny detail.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.840
The man Laurie decapitated wasn't actually
Michael.

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:03.220
It was a paramedic with a crushed larynx that
Michael had tricked her into thinking was

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:03.720
him.

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:07.440
Three years later, Laurie has convinced the
staff at Grace Andersen Sanitarium that she's

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:12.140
basically comatose while she waits for a final,
final showdown with her brother.

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:15.960
Things don't go as planned, and Laurie winds
up with a knife in her back before she plummets

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:17.220
off the hospital roof.

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:18.900
"I'll see you in Hell."

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:28.440
The focus then turns to the old Myers house,
where a group of college kids have agreed

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:30.300
to star in an investigative web series.

00:06:30.569 --> 00:06:34.780
Michael follows the group into the house and
proceeds to kill each hopeful internet star,

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:38.400
all in front of a live audience who assumes
for a good part of the night that everything

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:39.410
happening is fake.

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:44.200
When the Myers house is accidentally set ablaze,
Michael is trapped inside and supposedly dies.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:49.040
You may have thought Laurie Strode was out
for good, but 2018's Halloween made the decision

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:54.260
to retcon everything after the 1978 original,
which means that this time, there's no sibling

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:54.760
drama.

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:59.220
"Wasn't it her brother, who like cold-blooded
murdilated all those teenagers?"

00:06:59.400 --> 00:06:59.900
"No.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:03.140
That's just a bit that some people made up
to make them feel better I think."

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:07.660
And, most importantly, Laurie is very much
alive, although she's spent four decades living

00:07:07.669 --> 00:07:10.360
like the slasher movie equivalent of a Doomsday
prepper.

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:14.379
Michael has been locked up at Smith's Grove
Sanitarium, but after a pair of investigative

00:07:14.379 --> 00:07:18.910
reporters come to interview him, he decides
40 years is long enough behind bars and sets

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:21.860
out for a final face-off with the babysitter
that got away.

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:25.160
Laurie, on the other hand, has a strained
relationship with her daughter Karen, but

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:27.700
her granddaughter Allyson wants to mend fences.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:32.220
Everything changes when Michael returns, and
Laurie, Karen, and Allyson team up to take

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:32.720
him down.

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:37.200
It's discovered that Michael's psychiatrist,
Dr. Sartain, is obsessed with him and was

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:38.560
the one behind his escape.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:42.500
Eventually, the Strode clan defeats Michael
with the power of fire and firearms.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:43.240
"Gotcha."

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:49.340
But as we all know, there's probably no stopping
this psycho slasher.

